{# ---------- Focus statement ---------- #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="focus-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research focus</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="focus-title">Questions that cross borders</h2>
        <p class="lede">Social workers address society's greatest challenges at home and abroad. Our global research builds the partnerships and evidence to meet them.</p>
        <p>The Office of Global Engagement fosters collaboration between the School and universities, research institutions and organizations worldwide. Our faculty's international work concentrates in four areas:</p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><strong>Reconciliation and peace.</strong> How conflict and violence spread, what they cost, and how peacemaking and restorative justice can shape leaders, studied in Northern Ireland with Corrymeela.</li>
          <li><strong>Parenting and child well-being.</strong> Cultural adaptation and large-scale dissemination of a parenting intervention in Chile with Fundación San Carlos de Maipo, and co-teaching in Chile's first clinical master's program in social work.</li>
          <li><strong>Health equity and research capacity.</strong> Cortando la Brecha builds capacity among early- and mid-career Puerto Rican scholars responding to health and mental health disparities worsened by natural disasters and out-migration.</li>
          <li><strong>Workforce and education.</strong> Doctoral education and faculty exchange with Tallinn University in Estonia, and clinical faculty rotations that strengthen social work training in Chile.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="split__media">
        <blockquote class="pullquote">A global perspective makes us a humbler people and more accountable for our privileges.</blockquote>
        <figcaption class="pullquote-cite">Rubén Parra-Cardona, Ph.D., Professor and founding Associate Dean for Global Engagement</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Research areas ---------- #}
<section class="section section--sand" aria-labelledby="areas-title">
